; ============================================================================
; program.dmc — DMC-4080 startup program for the inkjet test rig
;
; This file is downloaded to the controller's non-volatile memory.  To update
; it, connect with Galil Composer (or telnet) and use:
;
;   gclib_set_program()  (gclib call)   — from the GUI's "Upload Program" button
;   BP              — burn program to non-volatile memory (see note below)
;   RS              — hardware reset the controller
;
; ── What this program does ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;   #AUTO runs automatically at power-up.  It:
;     1. Configures the stepper motor type for both active axes.
;     2. Enables both motors so they hold position immediately on power-up.
;
;   All motion, jetting, and solenoid control is commanded from the GUI;
;   no stored motion programs are used at runtime.
;
; ── Axes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;   A (alias X) — X-axis carriage    FUYU FSL30 linear stage + Nema 14 stepper
;   D           — Reservoir height   Shorter version of the same FSL30 stage
;
;   MT=2 : Stepper motor, active-low step pulse (standard for FSL30 + driver)
;
; ── Motor enable at startup ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;   SHA and SHD energise the steppers so the carriage does not drift when the
;   controller boots.  If you prefer to enable motors manually from the GUI,
;   comment these two lines out.
;
; ── Unused axes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;   B, C, E, F, G, H are not wired up.  Do not send SH or motion commands
;   to them; the controller will report an error.
; ============================================================================

; ── Solenoid I/O ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;   Port 22 drives the ink solenoid MOSFET gate.  This pin rests HIGH before
;   any Galil code runs (confirmed by measuring it powered but pre-#AUTO), so
;   CB 22 here only forces it low from the moment #AUTO executes onward — it
;   does NOT cover the brief window between power-on and #AUTO starting.
;   TEMPORARY: current driver stage is an N-type MOSFET, so "port high" energizes
;   the solenoid during that pre-#AUTO window. Fix pending: swap to a P-type
;   (high-side) MOSFET so "high" reads as off at the hardware level too. Once
;   that swap is done, replace CB 22 below with SB 22, or remove the line
;   entirely if the new driver's idle-high state alone is sufficient.
; ============================================================================

#AUTO
CO 15;    'Set all extended I/O to output
CB 22;    'Solenoid off
MTA=2;    'Axis A (X carriage): stepper, active-low step
MTD=2;    'Axis D (reservoir):  stepper, active-low step
CN 1;     'Limit Switch Polarity: active high
SHA;      'Enable X-axis motor on boot
SHD;      'Enable D-axis motor on boot
EN
